                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_413\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit (\"Add block/position convention to all distinct from operators\") adds a\nsecond, block/position-based implementation of the IS_DISTINCT_FROM scalar operator to\nevery type (Bigint, Boolean, Char, Color, Date, Double, Integer, Interval, Real,\nSmallint, Time, Timestamp, TimeWithTimeZone, TimestampWithTimeZone, Tinyint, Ip, Json,\nUnknown, Varbinary, Varchar, Array, Map, Row, etc.), explicitly stating that with the\nold (NULL_FLAG-convention) implementation \"it's no longer necessary to extract the value\nout of the Block in order to invoke 'distinct from' operator,\" and that this change \"is\nexpected to resolve [a] performance issue.\"\n\nThis means the bug being fixed is a performance regression caused by the original\nimplementation of the IS_DISTINCT_FROM operator, which forced every value to be\nextracted out of its Block (via readNativeValue/getObject and boxing into Object,\nplus IsNull flags) before invoking the comparison, instead of operating directly on\nBlock+position.\n\ncandidate_413 is the commit that originally introduced this exact NULL_FLAG-based\nIS_DISTINCT_FROM implementation across the entire codebase in one shot: it adds\n`@ScalarOperator(IS_DISTINCT_FROM)` / `public static boolean isDistinctFrom(...,\n@IsNull boolean leftNull, ..., @IsNull boolean rightNull)` methods to BigintOperators,\nBooleanOperators, CharOperators, ColorOperators, DateOperators, DoubleOperators,\nIntegerOperators, IntervalDayTimeOperators, IntervalYearMonthOperators, RealOperators,\nSmallintOperators, TimeOperators, TimeWithTimeZoneOperators, TimestampOperators,\nTimestampWithTimeZoneOperators, TinyintOperators, UnknownOperators, VarbinaryOperators,\nand also introduces ArrayDistinctFromOperator, MapDistinctFromOperator, and the\nDECIMAL_DISTINCT_FROM_OPERATOR, registering them all in FunctionRegistry. This is\nidentical in shape and scope to the \"before\" code shown throughout fix_commit_diff.txt\n(the code being replaced/removed), confirming candidate_413 is where the\nperformance-problematic value-extraction-based distinct-from implementation was first\nintroduced. No other candidate introduces this pattern (candidate_69 only lays the\ngroundwork for the general OperatorInfo/OperatorType framework but does not add any of\nthe per-type isDistinctFrom methods; later candidates in the 540s-570s range only touch\nindividual files incrementally, long after the pattern was already established).\n"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
